{p:c}{col:ffd100}“What is not written is lost.”{/col}{/p}

He stands a head taller than most of the visage-bearers in Valdrakken and moves like someone who has had to relearn how. His scales are a dull obsidian, chipped at the edges of the horns, and his eyes are the amber of a forge banked for the night.

He dresses in borrowed robes, still creased from the merchant's folding, and carries a satchel heavier than it has any right to be.

{h2:c}The Slumber{/h2}
Sealed with the rest of his kind in the Forbidden Reach, he woke to a world ten thousand years older than the one he remembered.

{h2:c}The Chalice{/h2}
An archival construct of {col:66efdc}Shadowlands{/col} make, bought from a broker who asked no questions and answered fewer. It remembers what he tells it, and nothing else.
